# Per-machine settings for the Taskfile. Copy to .env and edit; .env is
# git-ignored and holds secrets, so never commit it.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only the llm-* tasks read this file. No application reads it: apps get their
# configuration from ConfigMaps and Secrets in the cluster, which the llm-*
# tasks create from these values. The shell's own variables of the same names
# are IGNORED, so a key exported in your shell can never win over the one here.
# Format: one NAME=value per line; no inline comments; one pair of quotes around
# a value is removed; a line starting with # is off; an empty value is off.
#
# To switch a source off, comment its line out and run `task llm-enable` again:
# the source, its Secrets and its models-file entries are removed. `task
# llm-disable` removes all of them at once. Running either only touches what
# llm-enable itself created: it refuses to overwrite a Secret or key you made by
# hand and tells you which one.
#
# Every setting is optional. `task llm-status` shows which sources are usable on
# this machine, in the order the router prefers them:
#   1. Ollama on the local network   (LLM_LAN_OLLAMA_URL)
#   2. OpenRouter                    (OPENROUTER_API_KEY)
#   3. Vertex AI                     (LLM_VERTEX_ACCOUNT + LLM_VERTEX_PROJECT)
#   4. Ollama on this machine        (http://127.0.0.1:11434 unless set below)
# `task llm-enable` adds the usable ones to the apps in the dev cluster, and
# `task llm-disable` removes them again.

# 1. Ollama on another machine in the network. The address must be reachable
#    from this machine and from the cluster's pods. The machine must have the
#    gemma4:31b pulled (`ollama pull gemma4:31b`); it may serve other models too.
#    Leave empty to skip this source.
LLM_LAN_OLLAMA_URL=

# 2. OpenRouter API key (https://openrouter.ai/keys). Leave empty to skip this
#    source. It is stored only in a Secret of the dev cluster.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# 3. Vertex AI. The gcloud account must be logged in (`gcloud auth login`); a
#    short-lived access token (about one hour) is minted from it and stored in a
#    Secret of the dev cluster. Leave the account empty to skip this source.
LLM_VERTEX_ACCOUNT=
LLM_VERTEX_PROJECT=
# Default: us-central1
# LLM_VERTEX_LOCATION=us-central1

# 4. Ollama on this machine, if it does not listen on the default address.
# LLM_LOCAL_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
